        "original_id": "13a0048c-5abb-50e5-9030-bb4d8ede88d9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alma Wade\n- Products: F.E.A.R., SAS: Secure Tomorrow\n- Companies: Monolith Productions, Sierra Entertainment\n- Systems: Jupiter EX engine\n- Concepts: survival horror, first-person shooter, series mystery\n\nFacts:\n- In 2005, Monolith Productions introduced Alma Wade in the video game F.E.A.R.\n- Alma Wade is a major antagonist and key figure in the F.E.A.R. series.\n- The mystery of Alma Wade is central to the F.E.A.R. series.\n- F.E.A.R. First Encounter Assault Recon is a survival horror first-person shooter video game.\n- Monolith Productions developed F.E.A.R. First Encounter Assault Recon, and Sierra Entertainment published it.\n- SAS: Secure Tomorrow uses the Jupiter EX engine.\n- The Jupiter EX engine used in SAS: Secure Tomorrow is similar or possibly identical to the engine used in F.E.A.R.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "b4c6ed25-1283-583a-b0c0-dc29ac4f8f26",
        "text": "Page: Alma Wade. Sentence: Alma Wade is a major antagonist and key figure in the \"F.E.A.R.\" series of first-person shooter horror video games by Monolith Productions, introduced in \"F.E.A.R.\" in 2005.\nPage: Alma Wade. Sentence: The mystery of Alma is the very core of the series.\nPage: F.E.A.R.. Sentence: F.E.A.R. First Encounter Assault Recon is a survival horror first-person shooter video game developed by Monolith Productions and published by Sierra Entertainment.\nPage: SAS: Secure Tomorrow. Sentence: The game utilizes Jupiter EX engine, similar, if not identical to the one in F.E.A.R..",
